  {
   "id": "s4_0",
   "type": "text",
   "text": "#compare\n# 29 · #compare\n---\n### Today\n- slow\n- by hand\n- argued about\n---\n### Proposed\n- quick\n- from the model\n- the same every time\n",
   "x": 80,
   "y": 5120,
   "width": 1280,
   "height": 860
  },
  {
   "id": "s4_1",
   "type": "text",
   "text": "# 30 · +++ steps\nThe first frame is here.\n+++\nThis should arrive on the next press.\n+++\nAnd this one after it.\n",
   "x": 1600,
   "y": 5120,
   "width": 1280,
   "height": 860
  },
  {
   "id": "s4_2",
   "type": "text",
   "text": "#band\n# 31 · A table and a list\n---\n### The table\n| Thing | State |\n|---|---|\n| One | `built` |\n| Two | `next` |\n| Three | `after` |\n---\n### The list\n- A bullet\n- Another\n  - Nested under it\n1. Numbered\n2. And again\n",
   "x": 3120,
   "y": 5120,
   "width": 1280,
   "height": 860
  },
  {
   "id": "g4",
   "type": "group",
   "label": "E · The rest",
   "x": 0,
   "y": 5040,
   "width": 4480,
   "height": 1020
  },
  {
   "id": "deck",
   "type": "text",
   "text": "#deck\n\ntheme: Atlas/Themes/Paper.css\nheader: {deck}  ·  {section}  ·  {n}/{total}\nsection: title\n\n# Every combination\n**One card per thing Atlas claims to do, numbered, so a screenshot names\nitself**\n\n31 cards in five sections. Present it, photograph anything that looks wrong,\nand quote its number.\n",
   "x": 0,
   "y": -1100,
   "width": 12080,
   "height": 860
  }
